prince harry is ready to tell his story  on monday  book publisher penguin random house  announced they would be publishing a new  memoir written by the duke of sussex  here's what we know according to the  press release we can expect the book to  hit shelves sometime in 2022  it goes on to say that for the first  time terry plans to share the definitive  account of the experiences  adventures losses and life lessons that  have helped shape him  the prince also released a statement  about the forthcoming memoir  harry wrote i've worn many hats over the  years both literally and figuratively  and my hope is that in telling my story  the highs and lows  the mistakes the lessons learned i can  help show that no matter where we come  from  we have more in common than we think  harry goes on to call the memoir  a first-hand account of my life that's  accurate and  wholly truthful in addition we learned  harry will donate proceeds to charity  the announcement comes just weeks after  harry and william reunited  following a tense year in their  relationship well this has been a very  highly anticipated reunion because of  course it is the first time that we've  seen  the brothers on their own since  the fallout the brothers attended the  unveiling ceremony for a statue of their  mother princess diana  on what would have been her 60th  birthday well i thought harry looked  particularly jovial  i mean he was smiling for most of the  time william looked a little bit more  serious but  was still smiling and of course they  were very aware  that there was a camera and a  photographer trained on them for the  whole time  certainly it is it is harry's hope and i  think williams as well  that there will be a point where the  relationship is  is better harry has said himself that he  loves his brother but he recognizes that  it's going to take  time to heal and speaking to sources  close to william  i think it is going to take some time  the duke of cambridge is still  very bitter and very hurt by a lot of  what harry and megan said in that  interview  particularly those allegations of racism  that were leveled against the royal  family  so clearly it's going to take far more  than the funeral of their grandfather  and indeed the unveiling of this statue  i think for the relationship to be  anywhere near what it once was and  possibly it's ambitious  to expect that it ever will be what it  once was but i think they both recognize  that a fracture that divides key and  important members of the royal family  is something that can only be ultimately  damaging  to the monarchy i think there is every  chance that we will see the brothers  back together again but that may not be  for some time with the  covert pandemic of course with the  relationship i think still being  under some strain and it may not be  until june when it's widely expected  that the sussexes will be back for the  queen's platinum  jubilee celebrations to mark her 70th  year on the throne when it is expected  that all of her family will be there to  celebrate this milestone
 

